sequenceDiagram
    accTitle: M8 canary evidence sequence
    accDescr: A canary applies an exact digest, waits through the configured window, publishes liveness, and lets a downstream host apply or hold the same digest. Silence or a revert is never a pass.
    participant Can as Canary host
    participant J as Replicated journal
    participant H as Downstream host
    Can->>J: 1 · Apply X at digest D, t0
    Note over J: 2 · Wait canary_wait_hours (24h default/fallback)
    Can->>J: 3 · Liveness publish later record or heartbeat
    H->>J: 4 · Gate check X@D
    alt 5 · Outcome
        H->>H: Evidence + liveness → apply X
    else Canary silent or reverted
        H->>H: Hold X, reason canary-silent
    end
